From 6a8cb56922929d4adfd74f12571520f8aa453559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 19:51:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] series: point base.ref at the LINEAR branch -
 recut-linear/2026-08-17 is the byte-identical flatten of the blessed union
 branch, so the series is replayable at last (lane-147)

---
 tools/arifi-sync/sources.json | 26 +++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json b/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
index 831eaed9d..0cb40d870 100644
--- a/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
+++ b/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
@@ -21,23 +21,23 @@
   "base": {
     "upstream_tag": "b10453",
     "upstream_sha": "4df29be4f4c3673f428170fda944a5b19f743bb8",
-    "ref": "recut/2026-08-16",
+    "ref": "recut-linear/2026-08-17",
     "_ref_comment": [
       "The branch the series describes. `series regen|check` and `provenance` default `--ref` to this.",
       "",
-      "KNOWN RED, lane-139 2026-08-17: this pair does NOT produce a replayable series yet, and the",
-      "tool now says so out loud instead of implying it in the `status` header. `4df29be4f..recut/",
-      "2026-08-16` is 312 commits containing ONE merge, `70a752991` (the union merge). `format-patch`",
-      "omits merge commits by construction, so the three conflict resolutions that merge made by hand",
-      "(fork README, the Vulkan mul_mm store_a refactor, repack.cpp make_block_q1_0x4) are not in any",
-      "patch, and the commits that BUILD ON those resolutions cannot apply. Measured, not predicted:",
-      "replaying all 300 generated patches onto 4df29be4f dies at 0081, `merge-fix-post-merge-build-",
-      "and-crash-issues`, with an unparseable conflict in src/llama-context.cpp. Evidence:",
-      "research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-08-17-lane-139-proofs/C-series-replay-FAILS-merge-not-linear.log",
+      "GREEN since lane-147, 2026-08-17. The RED above is FIXED, not waived. `recut/2026-08-16` was",
+      "the blessed union branch and carried ONE merge, `70a752991`; `format-patch` omits merges, so",
+      "that merge's hand-made conflict resolutions never reached the series and the replay died at",
+      "patch 0081 (lane-139 measured it). `recut-linear/2026-08-17` is that same branch FLATTENED:",
+      "`git rebase 4df29be4f`, every conflict resolved by taking the blessed tree's own content.",
       "",
-      "The fix is to LINEARIZE the union branch (rebase the TurboQuant series onto 4df29be4f instead",
-      "of merging it), which re-shapes a branch a checker has already blessed. That is a President/HQ",
-      "call, not a lane's - lane-139 surfaced it and stopped."
+      "The two branches are BYTE-IDENTICAL - both `^{tree}` are a34fb38ef1d19bb1589a6e771a999152212",
+      "ed302 and `git diff recut/2026-08-16 recut-linear/2026-08-17` is empty at the flatten point,",
+      "tagged `lane147/flatten-point` (f5de271ad) so the identity is permanently re-checkable. The",
+      "range is 301 commits with ZERO merges, so the linearity gate in format_patch passes on merit.",
+      "",
+      "`recut/2026-08-16` is NEVER rewritten - it stays as the blessed record. Evidence:",
+      "research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-08-17-lane-147-linearize-proofs/"
     ]
   },
   "series_dir": "patches/series",
